SPI: Serial Peripheral Interface. Fast, simple, synchronous. One master (STM32), one or more slave.

STM32 (master)          Device (slave)
  SCK  ──────────────────► SCK    clock
  MOSI ──────────────────► MOSI   master out, slave in
  MISO ◄────────────────── MISO   master in, slave out
  NSS  ──────────────────► CS     chip select (active LOW)
  
  Four wires. The master generates the clock, so there’s no baud rate to agree on — speed is 
  whatever the master drives, up to the slave’s limit.
  
Master shift reg: [0xA5] ⇄ [0x3C] :Slave shift reg
After 8 clocks:   [0x3C]   [0xA5]

Consequence: to read a byte, you must send a byte.